{"explanation": "The unit responds to the exterior body of a single real road vehicle (car, pickup, ambulance or fire truck) seen whole from the side or three-quarter front, with the hood, cab windshield and side windows clearly outlined. It is strongest for boxy or classic vehicles, often red, parked on pavement. It is weak for interiors and cargo areas, toy models, tractors and other farm-style machines, cluttered scenes with several vehicles, and photos where people dominate or cover the car. Compared with similar units, it prefers clean side-profile road vehicles such as fire engines, police vans and school buses over tractors, convertibles full of people and odd utility bodies.", "predictions": [{"question": "How is the main vehicle shown?", "answers": ["whole exterior, side or three-quarter view", "whole exterior, straight front or rear view", "partial, crowded or cut-off exterior", "interior or cargo area, or no vehicle"], "most_active": "whole exterior, side or three-quarter view", "least_active": "interior or cargo area, or no vehicle"}, {"question": "Is the main vehicle a real full-size road car, truck or van (not a toy, model, tractor or farm machine)?", "answers": ["yes, real road vehicle", "toy, model, tractor or other non-road machine", "no vehicle visible"], "most_active": "yes, real road vehicle", "least_active": "toy, model, tractor or other non-road machine"}, {"question": "What is the dominant body color of the main vehicle?", "answers": ["red", "other single color", "multicolor or heavily decorated", "no vehicle visible"], "most_active": "red", "least_active": "multicolor or heavily decorated"}, {"question": "Do people take up a large part of the photo or cover the vehicle?", "answers": ["no people or only small background people", "people prominent or covering the vehicle", "no vehicle visible"], "most_active": "no people or only small background people", "least_active": "people prominent or covering the vehicle"}]}
```

